#   LAUNCH_TRAINER_SHA   sha256 of stack/scripts/v8f_mini_train.py at that commit: the tip's blob must hash to it
#   LAUNCH_MODEL_SHA     sha256 of stack/tanitad/models/v8f_mini.py at that commit: the tip's blob must hash to it
#   PREREG_SHA           sha256 of the LANDED PREREG_V8F_LAUNCH_INTENT v2 (the redesign): UNSET until it lands; the launch step fills it
#   READER_SHA           sha256 of the reader that scores the runs: UNSET until it is final; the launch step fills it
#   `python gen/make_chain_li.py --prereg-sha <64 hex> --reader-sha <64 hex>` rewrites exactly those lines (a pin not named keeps its value). While ANY of the five contains "<<UNSET", a REAL RUN REFUSES before anything is waited for, taken or shipped;
#   --check-tree refuses only a placeholder trainer / model pin (it checks a tree, which does not need the PREREG or the reader); --dry-run needs none and prints which are unset.
